    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d738">

                <pb facs="1452" n="1440" sameAs="frus:frus1945v02/pg1440"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.50/3–2145: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-03-22T00:00:00-04:00">March 22,
                            1945—midnight</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2222. Substance of Moscow’s 832 March 21 to the Department (repeated to London)
                    on EEC and ECO was informally communicated to the British Embassy March 22, with
                    indication that we felt this method preferable to their proposal to make
                    representations at Moscow.</p>
                <p>We are drafting comments on statement of relationship of EEC and ECO to economic
                    and social council as contained in your 2859 March 20.<anchor n="76"
                        xml:id="d738-f1"/> These will be forwarded to you together with a suggested
                    statement of our position on the reparations points referred to in your 2802
                    March 17.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Moscow.<anchor n="77" xml:id="d738-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d738-f1" n="76" xml:id="d738-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed: it contained a statement of British views (840.50/3–2045).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d738-f2" n="77" xml:id="d738-f2-content">
